{"diagnosis": "TRAP asserted with tohost FAIL 0xdead on 256-word NOP slide where no illegal instruction should trap and PC should progress. CYCLES=2009 shows fetch never retired correctly. Root cause is line 1446 `decoder_trigger <= mem_do_rinst || mem_done` which triggers decode on request OR completion instead of qualified completion, latching invalid rdata as opcode and causing illegal-instruction trap per picosoc/picosoc.v:146-156 cpu mem connection and picosoc/picosoc.v:144 ENABLE_IRQ context; trace wins.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -1446,3 +1446,3 @@
-		decoder_trigger <= mem_do_rinst || mem_done;
+		decoder_trigger <= mem_do_rinst && mem_done;
 		decoder_trigger_q <= decoder_trigger;
 		decoder_pseudo_trigger <= 0;", "expected": "tohost PASS with TRAP deasserted and fetch progress, checksum != c2a7a4d6295484feeb9ec1ea9381732b8e39a7ccd1997c7d70f6454da2fb4659"}

